#: inc/customizer.php:1062
msgid "Typography"
msgstr ""

#: inc/customizer.php:1064
msgid ""
"You can use this to update the default fonts using the fonts\n"
"        from the google fonts api (https://fonts.google.com/).  If you want "
"to add a new font, \n"
"        then you need to use the exact letter casing and spacing.  You "
"should be able to achieve this \n"
"        by copying and pasting the name of the font directly from the google "
"fonts site.  \n"
"        Because the Google font library is so large, you will\n"
"        find that some fonts are more compatible than others.  If you delete "
"all of the \n"
"        font names then your fonts will be set to default and will be hosted "
"locally."
